$$SYNTAX-LEVEL 2
*(mgdb-projects
<a class="mgdb-skip-link" href="#mgdb-projects-main">Skip to main content</a>
<main class="mgdb-page mgdb-hub-page mgdb-projects-page" id="mgdb-projects-main">

  <nav class="mgdb-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
    <a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">&rsaquo;</span><span aria-current="page">Projects</span>
  </nav>

  <section class="mgdb-hero-basic" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
    <span class="mgdb-hero-basic-icon" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 84 84" role="presentation" focusable="false">
        <rect x="12" y="44" width="12" height="26" rx="3" fill="currentColor" />
        <rect x="30" y="26" width="12" height="44" rx="3" fill="currentColor" />
        <rect x="48" y="36" width="12" height="34" rx="3" fill="currentColor" />
        <rect x="66" y="16" width="6" height="54" rx="3" fill="currentColor" />
        <rect x="8" y="72" width="66" height="5" rx="2.5" fill="#2f5e2a" />
      </svg>
    </span>
    <div>
      <h1 id="projects-title">Maize research projects</h1>
      <p>Projects whose data, results or documentation live at MaizeGDB: analyses run here, the sequencing and assembly projects whose genomes the site serves, and the long-running community resources it holds. Projects MaizeGDB itself runs carry the kernels from the site mark.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <nav class="mgdb-section-tabs" aria-label="Sections on this page">
    <a href="#projects-browse" class="is-current" aria-current="true">Search</a>
    <a href="#projects-about">About</a>
    <a href="#projects-related">Related resources</a>
  </nav>

  <section id="projects-browse" aria-labelledby="projects-browse-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="projects-browse-title">Search</h2></div>
    </div>
    <p class="projects-section-lead">Search by title, topic, or the group that runs it. Filtering happens as you type, and the filtered view can be shared from the address bar.</p>

    <div class="mgdb-search">
      <div class="mgdb-search-row">
        <div class="mgdb-field">
          <label class="mgdb-label" for="projects-query">Search projects</label>
          <p class="mgdb-hint" id="projects-query-hint">Enter a project name, a topic, or the group that runs it. Example: <code>NAM</code>, <code>insertions</code> or <code>Dooner</code></p>
          <input class="mgdb-input" id="projects-query" name="q" type="search" aria-describedby="projects-query-hint" autocomplete="off" placeholder="insertions" />
        </div>
        <button class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-quiet" id="projects-reset" type="button" hidden>Reset</button>
      </div>
      <div class="mgdb-filters">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="mgdb-small mgdb-muted">Kind:</span>
        $(topic-chips)
        <span class="mgdb-result-count" id="projects-count" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-card-grid projects-grid" id="projects-results">
      $(project-cards)
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-empty" id="projects-empty" hidden>
      <h3>No projects match that search</h3>
      <p>There are $(project-count) projects listed here. Clear the search and filters to see all of them.</p>
      <button class="mgdb-button mgdb-button-secondary" id="projects-empty-reset" type="button">Clear search and filters</button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="projects-about" aria-labelledby="projects-about-title">
    <div class="mgdb-prose-layout">
      <div class="mgdb-prose">
        <h2 id="projects-about-title" class="mgdb-leaf-heading">About</h2>
        <p>A project is a body of work with a beginning and an end, rather than a search interface. It answers a question over a fixed set of inputs, and its results do not change until the work is repeated. That makes it a different kind of page from the rest of the site: a <a href="/data_center/">data hub</a> searches the production database and returns whatever is in it today, and a <a href="/sitemap">tool</a> takes your input and computes an answer.</p>
        <p>Three kinds are listed here. <strong>MaizeGDB analyses</strong> are run and published here, each as one self-contained page carrying what was measured, what the numbers mean, how they were produced, and the files behind them, so a figure can always be traced back to a downloadable table. <strong>Genome projects</strong> are the sequencing and assembly efforts whose assemblies and annotations the site serves. <strong>Community resources</strong> are the mutant collections, maps and protocol sets that MaizeGDB hosts or documents on behalf of the groups that built them.</p>
        <p>A project keeps its page wherever that page already is. Several of these open a resource page or a data hub elsewhere on the site, and one opens the project's own website; the card says which before you click.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="mgdb-aside-card">
        <h3>Proposing a project</h3>
        <p>Analyses that would be useful to the maize community are welcome here, and so is documentation for a maize project that has nowhere else to put it. Get in touch through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a> with what you have and what it answers.</p>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="projects-related" class="mgdb-hub-related" aria-labelledby="projects-resources-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div>
        <h2 id="projects-resources-title">Related resources</h2>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-resource-panel">
      <div class="mgdb-resource-list">
        <a href="/data_center/">
          <strong>Data Hubs</strong>
          <span>Search the production database by record type, rather than a fixed result set</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/genome">
          <strong>Genome Data Hub</strong>
          <span>The assemblies and annotations these analyses are built on</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/ai">
          <strong>AI and machine learning</strong>
          <span>Model-ready datasets and predictions across the site</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/contact">
          <strong>Contact MaizeGDB</strong>
          <span>Propose an analysis, or ask about one that is published</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
          <strong>Bulk downloads</strong>
          <span>The wider download server these projects' files sit beside</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>
)
